# ssh-keygen — real-world examples

## Generate a modern Ed25519 key (recommended)

```sh
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "david@homelab"
```

## Generate a 4096-bit RSA key

```sh
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -C "david@homelab"
```

## Generate a key with a comment tagged to user and host

```sh
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "$USER@$HOSTNAME"
```

## Change the passphrase on an existing key

```sh
ssh-keygen -p -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

## Remove the passphrase from a key

```sh
ssh-keygen -p -P old_passphrase -N '' -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

## Show a key's fingerprint

```sh
ssh-keygen -lf ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

## Flag reference

| Flag       | What it does                              |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| -t type    | key type (ed25519, rsa, ecdsa)            |
| -b bits    | key size (RSA)                            |
| -C comment | label the key                             |
| -p         | change/remove the passphrase              |
| -N pass    | new passphrase ('' for none)              |
| -f file    | key file path                             |
| -lf file   | show fingerprint of a key                 |
